{"id":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_1","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.passage","labels":[{"language":"en","role":"preferred","value":"Tattvartha Sutra — Sutra 1.1 (Ratnatraya)"}],"extensions":{"textual":{"container":"mw:work:jainism:tattvartha-sutra","sequence":1,"unit":"sutra"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_1:sa","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_1","language":"sa","script":"Deva","representation":"source","text":"सम्यग्दर्शनज्ञानचारित्राणि मोक्षमार्गः ॥ १.१ ॥"},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_1:en","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_1","language":"en","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Right Faith (Samyag-Darshana), Right Knowledge (Samyag-Jnana), and Right Conduct (Samyag-Charitra) together constitute the path to Liberation (Moksha)."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_1:id","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_1","language":"id","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Keyakinan Benar (Samyag-Darshana), Pengetahuan Benar (Samyag-Jnana), dan Perilaku Benar (Samyag-Charitra) secara bersama-sama membentuk jalan menuju Pembebasan Sejati (Moksha)."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_2","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.passage","labels":[{"language":"en","role":"preferred","value":"Tattvartha Sutra — Sutra 1.2 (Right Faith)"}],"extensions":{"textual":{"container":"mw:work:jainism:tattvartha-sutra","sequence":2,"unit":"sutra"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_2:sa","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_2","language":"sa","script":"Deva","representation":"source","text":"तत्त्वार्थश्रद्धानं सम्यग्दर्शनम् ॥ १.२ ॥"},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_2:en","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_2","language":"en","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Right Faith is belief in the true nature of substances and realities as they truly are."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_2:id","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_2","language":"id","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Keyakinan Benar adalah kepercayaan yang teguh pada hakikat sejati dari segala realitas dan unsur keberadaan sebagaimana adanya."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_4","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.passage","labels":[{"language":"en","role":"preferred","value":"Tattvartha Sutra — Sutra 1.4 (Seven Tattvas)"}],"extensions":{"textual":{"container":"mw:work:jainism:tattvartha-sutra","sequence":3,"unit":"sutra"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_4:sa","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_4","language":"sa","script":"Deva","representation":"source","text":"जीवाजीवास्रवबन्धसंवरनिर्जरामोक्षास्तत्त्वम् ॥ १.४ ॥"},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_4:en","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_4","language":"en","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"The fundamental realities are: Soul (Jiva), Non-soul matter (Ajiva), Inflow of karma (Asrava), Bondage (Bandha), Influx stoppage (Samvara), Shedding of karma (Nirjara), and Liberation (Moksha)."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_4:id","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:1_4","language":"id","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Tujuh realitas fundamental keberadaan adalah: Jiwa (Jiva), Materi bukan-jiwa (Ajiva), Masuknya karma (Asrava), Keterikatan karma (Bandha), Penghentian aliran karma (Samvara), Pengikisan karma (Nirjara), dan Pembebasan Mutlak (Moksha)."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:5_21","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.passage","labels":[{"language":"en","role":"preferred","value":"Tattvartha Sutra — Sutra 5.21 (Parasparopagraho Jivanam)"}],"extensions":{"textual":{"container":"mw:work:jainism:tattvartha-sutra","sequence":4,"unit":"sutra"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:5_21:sa","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:5_21","language":"sa","script":"Deva","representation":"source","text":"परस्परोपग्रहो जीवानाम् ॥ ५.२१ ॥"},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:5_21:en","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:5_21","language":"en","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Souls render service to one another; the function of all living beings is to support and help each other."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:5_21:id","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:5_21","language":"id","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Jiwa-jiwa saling memberikan pelayanan dan pertolongan satu sama lain; fungsi hakiki dari segala makhluk hidup adalah saling menyokong dan menolong sesama."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:7_1","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.passage","labels":[{"language":"en","role":"preferred","value":"Tattvartha Sutra — Sutra 7.1 (Five Mahavratas)"}],"extensions":{"textual":{"container":"mw:work:jainism:tattvartha-sutra","sequence":5,"unit":"sutra"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:7_1:sa","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:7_1","language":"sa","script":"Deva","representation":"source","text":"हिंसानृतस्तेयाब्रह्मपरिग्रहेभ्यो विरतिर्व्रतम् ॥ ७.१ ॥"},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:7_1:en","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:7_1","language":"en","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"The vows consist in abstention from: Violence/Harm (Himsa), Falsehood (Anrita), Stealing (Steya), Unchastity (Abrahma), and Possessiveness/Attachment (Parigraha)."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:7_1:id","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:7_1","language":"id","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Ikrar-ikrar agung terdiri dari menahan diri dari: Kekerasan/Menyakiti makhluk lain (Himsa), Dusta/Kepalsuan (Anrita), Mengambil hak orang lain (Steya), Ketidaksucian/Hawa nafsu (Abrahma), dan Keterikatan pada kepemilikan duniawi (Parigraha)."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:10_1","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.passage","labels":[{"language":"en","role":"preferred","value":"Tattvartha Sutra — Sutra 10.1 (Kevala Jnana)"}],"extensions":{"textual":{"container":"mw:work:jainism:tattvartha-sutra","sequence":6,"unit":"sutra"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:10_1:sa","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:10_1","language":"sa","script":"Deva","representation":"source","text":"मोहक्षयाज्ज्ञानदर्शनावरणान्तरायक्षयाच्च केवलम् ॥ १०.१ ॥"},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:10_1:en","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:10_1","language":"en","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Upon the complete destruction of deluding karma, and the destruction of knowledge-obscuring, perception-obscuring, and obstructive karmas, infinite pure omniscience (Kevala Jnana) arises."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
{"id":"mw:content:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:10_1:id","record_type":"resource","kind":"textual.content","extensions":{"textual":{"target":"mw:passage:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:10_1","language":"id","script":"Latn","representation":"source","text":"Setelah sirnanya secara mutlak karma ilusi (Moha), serta hancurnya karma yang menutupi pengetahuan, persepsi, dan penghalang batin, memancarlah kemahatahuan mutlak yang tak terbatas (Kevala Jnana)."},"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:jainism:tattvartha-sutra-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:jainism:tattvartha-sutra:rec-2026"}}}
